<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sulla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 138–78 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Lucius Cornelius Sulla, Sulla Felix</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucius Cornelius Sulla was a Roman general and statesman. After serving in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurthine-war">Jugurthine War</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-war-91-87-bce">Social War</a>, he fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-mithridatic-war">First Mithridatic War</a> against Mithridates VI, sacking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> in 86 BCE. He then marched on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, won the civil war against the followers of Marius, and as dictator in 82–79 BCE carried out proscriptions and strengthened the Senate before retiring.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sulla.jpg" alt="Sulla" width="320" height="284" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Q._Pompeius_Rufus,_denarius,_54_BC,_RRC_434-1_(Sulla_only).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
